<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>{{ pages.kids.heading }}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ pages.kids.intro }}</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href="book.html">Book a first lesson &mdash; {{ lessons.first.price }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What I care about</h2>
    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Songs they recognise</h3>
        <p>Children practise music they like and avoid music they don&rsquo;t. That&rsquo;s not a discipline problem, it&rsquo;s just how it works &mdash; so we use it rather than fighting it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Exams are optional</h3>
        <p>If a student wants AMEB, we&rsquo;ll prepare properly and they&rsquo;ll do well. If they don&rsquo;t, they lose nothing. Grades are one path, not the point.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Proper foundations anyway</h3>
        <p>Reading, technique, rhythm and theory all get taught &mdash; just attached to music they care about, so it goes in without a fight.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>A note for parents</h2>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div>
        <p>Most children who quit an instrument quit because it stopped being fun before it started being satisfying. There&rsquo;s a gap in there &mdash; usually somewhere in the second year &mdash; and getting a student across it is most of the job.</p>
        <p>The way across is that they can already play something they&rsquo;re proud of. So that comes first, and the grind comes later, in small doses, once there&rsquo;s a reason for it.</p>
        <p>I&rsquo;ll tell you honestly how it&rsquo;s going. If your child isn&rsquo;t practising and isn&rsquo;t enjoying it, I&rsquo;d rather say so than take the money for another six months.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Practicalities</h3>
        <p><strong>Ages:</strong> from around 7<br>
        <strong>Where:</strong> my home studio, {{ site.location }}<br>
        <strong>When:</strong> {{ site.days }}, after school or earlier<br>
        <strong>Length:</strong> 30 minutes for children, 30&ndash;60 for teenagers<br>
        <strong>Cost:</strong> {{ lessons.child.price }} for {{ lessons.child.length | replace(" min", " minutes") }}<br>
        <strong>Parents:</strong> welcome to sit in, or to wait elsewhere &mdash; some children play better without an audience</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Teenagers</h2>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div>
        <p>Teenagers usually know exactly what they want to play, and the fastest way to lose them is to ignore that.</p>
        <p>If they&rsquo;re into songwriting, we&rsquo;ll do harmony and composition. If they&rsquo;re in a band, we&rsquo;ll do chords, feel and playing with other people. If they want to audition for a music course, that&rsquo;s a specific job and I&rsquo;ve prepared students for it.</p>
        <p>Longer lessons tend to suit them better &mdash; an hour gives room to actually get somewhere.</p>
      </div>
      {%- set quote = (testimonials | forPage("kids"))[0] %}
      <div>
        {%- if quote %}
        <blockquote class="pull">
          &ldquo;{{ quote.quote }}&rdquo;
          <cite>{{ quote.name }}</cite>
        </blockquote>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap narrow" style="text-align:center">
    <h2>Start with one lesson</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin:0 auto">{{ lessons.first.length | replace(" min", " minutes") }}, {{ lessons.first.price }}, no obligation. It&rsquo;s as much about whether they get on with me as anything else.</p>
    <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content:center">
      <a class="btn" href="book.html">Book a first lesson</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
